      "attributes": {
        "id": 434,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "These are both humble forms used to describe one's own actions politely. お～する is used with regular verbs, such as 手伝う 'help' becoming お手伝いする (same meaning, but in a deferential sense). In contrast, いたす is the humble form of する and is used instead of お～する when using する itself. For example, 連絡いたします 'I will contact you.' is the humble form of 連絡する (same meaning).",
